5562 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515562 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $15{\\text{i}}^{4}+15{\\text{i}}^{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515562 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7700df8a-7603-5144-96dd-4cda2bbcc154" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515562 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the first few powers of $\\text{i},$ where $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{i}}^{0} & =1 \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{1} & =\\text{i} \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{3} & ={\\text{i}}^{2}\\cdot \\text{i}=(-1)\\cdot \\text{i}=-\\text{i} \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{4} & ={\\text{i}}^{2}\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{2}=(-1)\\cdot (-1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{\\text{i}}^{4}+15{\\text{i}}^{2}=15(1)+15(-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515577 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515577 #edb/ref 1069 "q-921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515577 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515577 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of ${\\text{i}}^{7}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515577 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "963c1f30-8cab-5b1e-a22e-507ad07f1c0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515577 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=7.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n7÷4=1\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{7}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515584 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515584 #edb/ref 1069 "q-536" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515584 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515584 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify ${({\\text{i}}^{3})}^{10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515584 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a99262a6-2443-5dc5-a1ae-4680319ed028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515584 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{({\\text{i}}^{3})}^{10}={\\text{i}}^{3\\cdot 10}={\\text{i}}^{30}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=30.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n30÷4=7\\,\\text{R}2.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{30}={\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515613 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515613 #edb/ref 1069 "q-554" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515613 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515613 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify ${\\text{i}}^{27}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515613 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e97c4d66-5268-5c26-8025-6f1540da8cb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515613 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=27.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n27÷4=6\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{27}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515616 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515616 #edb/ref 1069 "q-535" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515616 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515616 #edb/ref 1071 "If $a={\\text{i}}^{5},$ then ${a}^{3}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515616 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee98c1bb-35f5-5014-9747-c74bb8f7a21e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515616 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}={({\\text{i}}^{5})}^{3}={\\text{i}}^{5\\cdot 3}={\\text{i}}^{15}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=15.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n15÷4=3\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{15}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515618 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515618 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515618 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515618 #edb/ref 1071 "$-5{\\text{i}}^{-1}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515618 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd293abd-5e28-58d2-85df-2177162157d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515618 #edb/ref 1074 "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n-5{\\text{i}}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\text{i}}=-\\frac{5}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=-\\frac{5\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n-\\frac{5\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=-\\frac{5\\text{i}}{(-1)}=-\\frac{5}{(-1)}\\cdot \\text{i}=5\\text{i}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
